  "explanation": {
    "short": "The letters ข ส ห ฝ ถ ผ (and a few rare ones) are the \"high class\". A live syllable that starts with a high-class letter and has no mark rises, like the end of a question: ขา, หู and สอง go up, while ตา and ดี stay level.",
    "more": "The sounds: ข and ถ and ผ are k, t and p with a puff of air (kh, th, ph), ส is s, ห is h, ฝ is f. Rising starts a little low and climbs, like a curious \"Oh?\". Compare ตา (eye, mid tone) with ขา (leg, rising tone): the vowel is the same, only the class of the first letter differs. The letter อ here is a vowel: สอง is \"sawng\". The word ผม is both \"hair\" and a man's word for \"I\", and it rises."
  },
